pages.Silence:
[[File:Last Word icon.png|frame|<sm2>weapons_silence.mp3</sm2> Silence!]]
{{Quotation|Silencer|This will shut you up.|sound=vo_silencer_silen_kill_14.mp3}}
'''Silence''' is a status effect that prevents those affected from using active hero abilities for the duration of the silence. It can be useful when ganking a hero with a blink or invisibility spell, as silences tend to have longer duration than other disables giving more time to kill the enemy. Silences in teamfights can also be very effective even for a short period of time, as they prevent the enemy from using their spells in combination with one another. Silencing an opponent also stops any channeling spells that they are currently using.

== Definition ==
{| <section begin=Definition /> class="wikitable" width="70%" style="text-align:center;"
! style="width:20%;" | Ability and Item<br>Disables
! style="width:60%;" | Disabled Aspect / Definition
! style="width:20%;" | Examples
|-
! [[Silence]]
| style="text-align:left;" | 
* Fully prevent any active abilities order, except item casts.
* [[Abilities#Autocast|Autocast abilities]] that are currently set to {{Key special|Autocast}} have their functionality disabled.
* [[Abilities#Toggle|Toggled abilities]] are stuck in their current {{Key special|Onoff}} state for the duration, but their functionality is not disabled.
| {{A|Global Silence|Silencer}}
|-
! [[Break]]
| style="text-align:left;" | 
* Fully disable passive abilities, does not disable any item passives and {{Symbol|Talent}} [[Talent]]s (with some exceptions).
* On-death passives (e.g. {{A|Reincarnation|Wraith King}}) and direct-synergy passives ({{Symbol|Aghanim}} {{A|Burrowstrike|Sand King|text=Caustic Finale with Burrowstrike}}) are generally not disabled.
| {{A|Viper Strike|Viper}}
|-
! [[Mute]]
| style="text-align:left;" |  
* Fully prevent item cast orders, except ability casts.
| {{A|Doom|Doom}}
<section end=Definition />
|}

== Mechanics ==
{{See also|Break}}
[[File:Silence example.png|thumb|Queen of Pain attempting to cast an ability while silenced. A grid layer covers the ability icons while silenced.]]
When a unit is silenced, the ability icons in its [[HUD]] are overlayed by a grid-like effect. {{Key press|mouseleft}} on an active ability or pressing its hotkey displays the word <code>Silenced</code> in red on the screen.

Silence disables every active ability, including toggle abilities and [[active attack modifiers]]. If an ability is being [[channeled]], silence cancels it immediately. If an ability is {{Key press|Toggled/On}}, Silence only prevents the player from toggling it off. If the toggle ability drains mana and the unit runs out of mana while silenced, the ability is Toggled {{Key special|Off}} normally.

Silence does not stop the effects of already cast abilities. For example, silencing {{H|Razor}} after he has already cast {{A|Static Link|Razor}} or {{A|Eye of the Storm|Razor}} does not stop the link from draining or the storm from striking.

Silence does not disable any passive ability. Although silence prevents, for example, the caster from using the active part of {{A|Vampiric Spirit|Wraith King}}, it does not stop him from gaining skeleton charges or the lifesteal to proc. Even when a passive ability has a cooldown or mana cost, silence never affects them in any way.

{{clr}}
=== Abilities Castable When Silenced ===
Few abilities with <code>DOTA_ABILITY_BEHAVIOR_IGNORE_SILENCE</code> flag are still castable when silenced. Silence also can not prevent them [[channeling]] and starting the ability's [[cast point]].
