[[File:Nightmare icon.png|frame]]
{{Quotation|Bane|See you in your dreams.|sound=vo_bane_bane_move_16.mp3}}
<section begin=Intro />'''Sleep''' is a rare status effect that completely disables those affected for the entire duration. However, units affected can be awaken by dealing damage to them.<section end=Intro />

Units affected cannot be woken up while they are [[invulnerable]]. Certain sleep sources turn the affected units invulnerable, making it impossible to wake them up. Units affected are also never automatically attacked by any unit, regardless of [[Settings#auto attack|auto attack]] settings. Hence, [[lane creeps]], [[neutral creeps]], and [[buildings]] will never attack sleeping units automatically because they are always using auto-attack.

[[Taunt]] sources can still force them to attack sleeping units. Player-controlled units do not automatically attack sleeping units either. The player can force their units to attack by selecting them as an attack target (with {{Key press|A}} or {{Key press|mouseleft}}).

Units affected are also not considered as targets from the following abilities:
